warning[W0318]: the default extends over `+ extra`
  --> corpus/lints/else_arithmetic.lu:24:40
   |
24 |     let swallowed = to_num("x") else 0 + extra
   |                                        ^ computed on the fallback, not on the value
   |
   = note: `else` binds loosest, so the fallback is the whole operator chain after it: this reads
     `to_num("x") else (0 + extra)`, and the default swallows the `+ extra`. Group the value
     if the default was meant to end at itself — the edit below is that grouping.
   = note: in a fallible function the clean spelling removes the `else` altogether: `to_num("x")?`
     propagates the failure and the arithmetic reads as written.
help: to default first and compute second, group the `else`
   |
24 |     let swallowed = (to_num("x") else 0) + extra
   |

